cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research proposal, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "BandGap-TH: Bandwidth versus Companding in Thai Audio Deepfake Detection under Telephone-Band Conditions"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "punyo_o"
repository-code: "https://github.com/punyopan/ysc"
url: "https://github.com/punyopan/ysc"
license: MIT
version: 0.5.0
date-released: 2026-08-19
abstract: >-
  A research proposal estimating how bandwidth reduction and logarithmic
  companding contribute to degradation in Thai audio-deepfake detection under
  simulated G.711 conditions. The study measures detection performance across
  low-pass cutoff frequencies and tests whether training with band-limited
  audio recovers some of the lost performance.
keywords:
  - audio deepfake detection
  - Thai speech
  - bandwidth limitation
  - companding
  - G.711
  - telephone speech
  - data augmentation
  - anti-spoofing
